{
 "_doc": "Socket gems (Loot Overhaul Phase 5, roadmap Socket-system-for-weapons). DRAFT catalogue, admin review pending. A gem is one family x one tier; its blueprint is sgem_<family>_<tier> (generated by gen-loot-tables.py --apply). Activated onto an item with an open socket, it RAISES a permanent property of its family by steps[tier] rungs of its ladder (cost-table rows, weakest first; the last rung is the cap), or adds that property at rung steps[tier]-1 when the item has none. affixes = loot/affixes.json ids whose (type, subtype) the gem merges into, in preference order; the item's category picks which is created (the first whose cats include it), and the gem only fits items whose category one of them allows. An existing value that is not on the ladder is placed by power (average damage for damage dice) and the result must be stronger, or the gem is refused and NOT consumed. Hard caps (the gate enforces them): damage <= 2d10 (iprp_damagecost row 13), enhancement/attack <= +16. The damage ladder skips flat +5 (admin 2026-11-06). Socketing is permanent; the gem is consumed. tiers = the rarity indices (colour from rarity.json) with the word that names the cut. drops: a gem's tier is a rarity roll (rarity.json weights + upgrades) at max(source floor, the level band's floor), capped at the band's ceiling; the family is weighted by weight. model = ModelPart1 on base 24 (miscsmall), chosen from the icon sheet (CLAUDE-item-appearances.md). value = AddCost gp of a gem of that tier.",
